WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:23.750
Resident Evil 7 is capcom’s attempt to make
its beloved horror franchise scary again,

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:29.289
by taking the series original formula of claustrophobic
locations and limited ammo and mixing it with

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:33.210
newer horror concepts like first person cat
and mouse chases.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:44.370
This first person perspective also allows
for a new way to play, Virtual Reality.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:49.629
Resident Evil 7 is a big deal for VR because
unlike Batman Arkham VR or whatever that Final

00:00:49.629 --> 00:00:52.940
Fantasy XV thing is, this isn't a short experience.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:56.329
RE7 is a big budget AAA numbered sequel.

00:00:56.329 --> 00:01:01.320
So I saw a golden opportunity by playing the
entirety of RE7 in PSVR.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.170
The whole thing.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:08.530
Which means experiencing moments like this.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:13.350
And this.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:22.509
And this.

00:01:22.509 --> 00:01:27.100
The game does a good job offering several
adjustable options in VR like Field of View,

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.540
walking speed, and crouch.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:32.860
The big thing is camera rotation options but
I’ll admit that none of them are perfect.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:37.520
On the default setting, the camera snaps at
angles of 30, 45, and 90 degrees.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:41.719
This is the safest option if you want to minimize
the risk of motion sickness but the jerky

00:01:41.719 --> 00:01:44.140
nature of it took me out of the experience.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:48.560
The option I used is called smoothing and
while I felt a little sick at first I was

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.299
able to get used to it and play the whole
game this way.

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:55.710
I would seriously advise caution though when
trying this setting and if you're prone to

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:58.659
motion sickness, I would avoid it all together.

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:02.670
Issues like this are partially due to the
fact that Resident Evil 7 isn’t designed

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:06.299
to be VR only, it has to work as a traditional
game too.

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:10.359
That means no use of Playstation Move controllers
to simulate your hands.

00:02:10.359 --> 00:02:13.430
The most you get is the camera is now controlled
by your head.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:18.450
So Resident Evil’s Virtual Reality is less
about enhancing the gameplay experience and

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.370
more about immersing you in its environments.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:25.920
The true strength of playing something in
VR is the sense of presence you gain.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.410
You are more aware of what's around you and
what's behind you.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:36.519
You can tell how long a hallway is and how
close an enemy is with greater accuracy.

00:02:36.519 --> 00:02:39.470
You really feel like you are walking around
this mansion.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:43.930
And Resident Evil 7 is the perfect game for
this because its environmental design and

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.930
art are top notch.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.210
The realistic art style fits perfectly.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:52.840
Every room is full of notes to read, pictures
to look at, and the disgusting imagery, my

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:56.620
god it's almost to gross to look at sometimes.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:01.940
This game is gnarly and fantastically disgusting
regardless of how you play it but being able

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:06.870
to see it so up close without that disconnect
between you and the TV makes your stomach

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:11.180
churn.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:18.480
Now let's talk about everyone’s favorite
part, the scares.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.459
There are plenty of those in your face jump
scares that will get you for sure, but for

00:03:22.459 --> 00:03:27.079
me the memorable moments come from entering
a new location for the first time and just

00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:28.790
having to walk through it.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:33.150
You have no idea what's gonna happen next
and that is just the worst feeling.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:36.269
I hated, and i mean hated the Old House.

00:03:36.269 --> 00:03:40.780
Its dark, its rotting, and I seriously wanted
to take the headset off when the giant bugs

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.579
showed up.

00:03:43.579 --> 00:03:54.090
We’d be here all day if I mentioned every
memorable moment but a few stand out scares

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:59.240
include; crawling inside this wall full of
centipedes.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:06.910
Walking through neck high water, the entirety
of this location.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:10.820
After beating the game I went back and played
outside of VR to see if there are any differences

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.380
and the answer is yes.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:16.650
For one it's way easier in my opinion to shoot
in VR because you can aim with your head.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:21.169
This might make the game slighter easier in
VR but I never found the difficulty balance

00:04:21.169 --> 00:04:24.220
to be an issue when playing.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:28.490
This also means if you freak out or try and
look away it messes up your shot which is

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:29.490
pretty neat.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:33.860
Side Note: It is possible to use your added
camera moment from VR to slightly break the

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.050
illusion of some scenes.

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:41.220
It doesn’t ruin anything but it's pretty
funny.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.790
Another thing is that a lot of character animations
are absent in VR.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:48.340
Stuff like getting knocked down or jumped
by an enemy doesn’t happen.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:52.370
This is most likely because taking camera
control away from you for even a moment would

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:54.280
induce motion sickness.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:58.710
Having played it in VR first I never missed
these animations or noticed their absence,

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.270
but playing it again I was surprised how many
of them were taken out.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:06.340
Of course sometimes the game can’t cut scripted
moments when they are story related.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:10.990
So to avoid motion sickness the game jarringly
switches to you floating in a black void with

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.030
a screen playing a pre-rendered cutscene in
front of you.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:18.280
It's the worst part of the VR experience in
that it quickly reminds you that you are playing

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.780
a video game.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:24.159
Perhaps the strangest part of playing Resident
Evil 7 a second time without VR is that I

00:05:24.159 --> 00:05:28.129
think playing in VR first actually kinda ruined
the game for me.

00:05:28.129 --> 00:05:30.770
It’s like when you go back and look at vacation
photos.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:33.479
It's the same thing, but everything is flat
now.

00:05:33.479 --> 00:05:34.860
You aren’t there in the same way.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.889
There's a real lack of punch to it.

00:05:36.889 --> 00:05:41.180
Don’t get me wrong I still think Resident
Evil 7 is a great game but this is a weird

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:46.510
and slightly amusing issue that I think a
lot of people who play this in VR first will

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:47.510
experience.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:51.240
You might also be wondering what it's like
to play a 9 hour game from start to finish

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.240
in VR?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:56.159
Well I wouldn’t recommend playing it all
in one day like I did because at the end of

00:05:56.159 --> 00:06:00.419
the night my eyes felt really awful after
having a screen stuck to them all day.

00:06:00.419 --> 00:06:02.020
But other than that I felt fine.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:05.260
You’d think I’d have wanted to take a
break to save my heart from all the tension

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:14.770
and scares but honestly I was enjoying the
game so much I just kept wanting to play it.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:23.509
My first playthrough of Resident Evil 7 is
gonna stick with me as one of those memorable

00:06:23.509 --> 00:06:27.229
gaming experiences partly due to playing it
VR.

00:06:27.229 --> 00:06:31.199
Even if it's not a perfect example of how
the technology can reshape games as we know

00:06:31.199 --> 00:06:35.699
them, getting to see the Baker Mansion for
the first time that way is something you only

00:06:35.699 --> 00:06:41.099
get one chance at and if you have the opportunity
to experience it this way, I highly recommend

00:06:41.099 --> 00:06:47.520
it.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:51.580
By the way if you are interested in just watching
a bunch of people get scared playing Resident

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:56.139
Evil 7 in VR, there is a video where I threw
some GameSpot employees into a room for your

00:06:56.139 --> 00:07:02.060
enjoyment.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:06.020
And If you have played Resident Evil 7 in
VR or if you want to try it now let me know

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:18.719
in the comments.

